-- Source module: Solutions.KFMB0
/-!
# The permutation-free `B̃₀ = D̃' J̃' C̃`

`B0approx` is the base `Bapprox` (HvdH Proposition 4.7(ii)) without its two data permutations
`P̃_t` and `P̃_s⁻¹`: `Bapprox = P̃_s⁻¹ ∘ B0approx ∘ P̃_t` (`Bapprox_eq`). Lemma 19 (κ, §8.1) keeps
both permutations in the transform, so the machine applies `B0approx` (see `KFMR19`, `KFMBap0`).
