/-!
# Item 12 (machine side, part 1): the permutation-free `B̃₀` slice program

Lemma 19 (κ, §8.1) keeps both permutations `P_s`, `P_t` in the transform. So the machine
applies `B̃₀ = D̃' J̃' C̃` (`B0approx`), not the base `B̃ = P̃_s⁻¹ B̃₀ P̃_t` that nlogn's `bapP`
computes. This file drops the two `permP` passes from `bapP`:

* `b0L`: the list form (`(List.range s).map (B0approx …)`), with `b0L_eq` (the pipeline
  `dapL ∘ japL ∘ cselL`) and the bound `b0L_LB`.
* `bapP0 = C̃-stage; JP; D̃'-stage` with `bapP0_run` and `bapP0_okc` (cost `bap0Cost`).
* `bap0SlP` (relocated by nlogn's `σP`, then transferred `bI → bO`) and `bap0Sl`, a
  `GL.LProg` in the same context `CtxB` as nlogn's `bapSl`.

